WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.208
Text Structure and Purpose

00:00:02.588 --> 00:00:04.128
Ask what the author is DOING.

00:00:05.328 --> 00:00:06.327
How to spot it

00:00:06.727 --> 00:00:10.041
The question says “main purpose” or “overall structure”

00:00:10.591 --> 00:00:12.263
Or one underlined sentence

00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:16.400
It’s testing: the job each part of a text is doing

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.395
The method

00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:21.878
Step 1: Label each sentence with a verb

00:00:22.158 --> 00:00:25.892
introduces, describes, challenges, concludes

00:00:26.442 --> 00:00:29.319
Step 2: Purpose = the main action

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:31.224
One verb for the whole text.

00:00:31.774 --> 00:00:35.170
Step 3: Structure = the actions in order

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.806
Belief, then evidence against it.

00:00:38.356 --> 00:00:40.472
Step 4: Check every word

00:00:40.752 --> 00:00:42.629
One wrong verb kills the choice.

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:44.289
In a few words

00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:47.408
Label. Combine. Check every word.

00:00:48.608 --> 00:00:49.509
Verb check

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:51.287
Describe ≠ argue

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.284
Informing is not persuading.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.281
Question ≠ refute

00:00:55.561 --> 00:00:57.116
Doubting is not disproving.

00:00:57.666 --> 00:00:59.344
Function, not content

00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:02.129
What the sentence does, not what it says.

00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:03.844
Two-part answers

00:01:04.124 --> 00:01:05.576
Both halves must be right.

00:01:06.776 --> 00:01:07.817
Let’s try one

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.385
Many people believe that goldfish have a memory span of only a few seconds.

00:01:13.385 --> 00:01:16.180
Experiments tell a different story.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:22.290
In one study, goldfish were trained to push a lever for food at a particular time of day;

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.343
months later, they still approached the lever at that hour.

00:01:26.343 --> 00:01:32.099
Such results suggest that goldfish memory is far more durable than commonly assumed.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:36.061
Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?

00:01:36.711 --> 00:01:40.471
Label each sentence. First, a common belief.

00:01:41.021 --> 00:01:42.931
Then, evidence against it.

00:01:43.481 --> 00:01:44.980
Then, a conclusion.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.818
Belief, evidence, conclusion. Only B has all three, in order.

00:01:52.018 --> 00:01:53.013
Common traps

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.247
Wrong verb

00:01:54.527 --> 00:01:56.872
“Argues” when the author only describes.

00:01:57.422 --> 00:01:58.283
Half right

00:01:58.563 --> 00:02:01.099
First part right, second part wrong.

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:03.907
Text Structure and Purpose

00:02:04.187 --> 00:02:07.156
Label. Combine. Check every word.

00:02:07.706 --> 00:02:08.479
Spot it

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:13.227
“main purpose”, “overall structure”, or an underlined sentence

00:02:13.777 --> 00:02:14.485
Steps

00:02:14.685 --> 00:02:17.163
1. Label each sentence with a verb

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:19.801
2. Purpose = the main action

00:02:20.081 --> 00:02:22.905
3. Structure = the actions in order

00:02:23.185 --> 00:02:25.473
4. Check every word of the choice

00:02:26.023 --> 00:02:26.776
Remember

00:02:26.976 --> 00:02:28.354
describe ≠ argue

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.080
question ≠ refute

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.156
Function = what it does, not what it says

00:02:33.436 --> 00:02:35.953
Two-part answers: both halves right

00:02:36.503 --> 00:02:37.108
Trap

00:02:37.308 --> 00:02:39.653
“Argues” when the author only describes

00:02:40.403 --> 00:02:44.097
